[{"location":"SISLens/#LensFactory.Lenses.init_SISLens","page":"SIS Lens","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.init_SISLens","text":"init_SISLens(D_d::Real=NaN, x_c::Real=0.0, y_c::Real=0.0, v_d::Real=NaN)\n\nInitialize a Singular Isothermal Sphere (SIS) lens with the given parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"Constants/#LensFactory.Constants","page":"Constants","title":"LensFactory.Constants","text":"Constants\n\nTesting :-)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"Constants/#Natural-constants","page":"Constants","title":"Natural constants","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants/","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"CONST_C = 299792458.0                        # meters/s\nCONST_G = 6.6743E-11                         # m^3 kg/s^2","category":"page"},{"location":"Constants/#Solar-constants","page":"Constants","title":"Solar constants","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants/","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"MASS_SUN = 1.988409870698051E+30             # kg\nRADIUS_SUN = 695700000.0                     # meters\nLUMINOSITY_SUN = 3.828E26                    # Watts = Joule/s","category":"page"},{"location":"Constants/#Distance-units","page":"Constants","title":"Distance units","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants/","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"DIST_PC = 3.0856775714409184E+16             # meters\nDIST_KPC = 3.0856775714409184E+19            # meters\nDIST_MPC = 3.0856775714409184E+22            # meters\nDIST_GPC = 3.0856775714409184E+25            # meters","category":"page"},{"location":"Constants/#Angular-units","page":"Constants","title":"Angular units","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants/","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"ANGLE_MICROARCSEC= 4.848136811095361E-12     # radians\nANGLE_MILLIARCSEC= 4.84813681109536E-09      # radians\nANGLE_ARCSEC = 4.84813681109536E-06          # radians\nANGLE_ARCMIN = 0.0002908882086657216         # radians\nANGLE_DEGREE = 0.017453292519943295          # radians","category":"page"},{"location":"Constants/#Temporal-units","page":"Constants","title":"Temporal units","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants/","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"YEAR2SECOND = 31557600.0                     # Seconds in a year\nYEAR2HOUR = 8766.0                           # Hours in a year\nYEAR2DAY = 365.25                            # Days in a year\nDAY2HOUR = 24.0                              # Hours in a day\nDAY2SECOND = 86400.0                         # Seconds in a day","category":"page"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology","text":"Cosmology\n\nTesting :-)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"Cosmology/#Initialization","page":"Cosmology","title":"Initialization","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.init_cosmology","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.init_cosmology","text":"init_cosmology(H0::RV=70.0, w::RV=-1.0, Omega_m0::RV=0.3, Omega_r0::RV=0.0, Omega_w0::RV=0.7)\n\nAn Abstract type to initialize a given cosmology.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"Cosmology/#Basics","page":"Cosmology","title":"Basics","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.scale_factor","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.scale_factor","text":"scale_factor(z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the scale factor (a) at redshift z. The formula is,\n\na = frac11+z\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.Ez","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.Ez","text":"Ez(z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the dimensionless Hubble parameter (E) at redshift, z.  The formula is,\n\nE(z) = sqrt Omega_m0 (1+z)^2 + Omega_r0 (1+z)^4 + Omega_k0 (1+z)^2 + Omega_w0 (1+z)^3(1+w) \n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_parameter","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_parameter","text":"hubble_parameter(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the Hubble parameter (H) at redshift z in rm mathbfkmsMpc.  The formula is,\n\nH(z) = H_0E(z)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#Time","page":"Cosmology","title":"Time","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_time","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_time","text":"hubble_time(H0::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the Hubble time (t_H) in rm mathbfGyr. The formula is,\n\nt_H = frac1rm H_0\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.age","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.age","text":"age(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the age (t_rm age) of the Universe at redshift z in rm mathbfGyr. The formula is,\n\nt_rm age(z) = int_z^infty frac1(1+z)H(z) dz \n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.lookback_time","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.lookback_time","text":"lookback_time(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates lookbak time (t_L) to a given redshift z in rm mathbfGyr. The formula is,\n\nt_L(z) = int_0^z frac1(1+z)H(z) dz \n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#Density-parameters","page":"Cosmology","title":"Density parameters","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.rho_cz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.rho_cz","text":"rho_cz(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the critical density (rho_c) of the Universe at redshift z in rm mathbfkgm^3. The formula is,\n\nrho_c(z) = frac3 H^2(z)8 pi rm G \n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_mz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_mz","text":"Omega_mz(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the matter density parameter (Omega_m) at redshift z. The formula is,\n\nOmega_m(z) = Omega_m(0)  (1+z)^3 left( fracH0H(z) right)^2\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_rz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_rz","text":"Omega_rz(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the matter density parameter (Omega_r) at redshift z. The formula is,\n\nOmega_r(z) = Omega_r(0)  (1+z)^4 left( fracH_0H(z) right)^2 \n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_wz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_wz","text":"Omega_wz(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the dark energy density parameter (Omega_w) at redshift z. The formula is,\n\nOmega_w(z) = Omega_w0 (1+z)^3(1+w) left( fracH_0H(z) right)^2 \n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_kz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_kz","text":"Omega_kz(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the curvature density parameter (Omega_k) at redshift z. The formula is,\n\nOmega_k(z) = Omega_k0 (1+z)^2 left( fracH_0H(z) right)^2 \n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#Distances","page":"Cosmology","title":"Distances","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_distance","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_distance","text":"hubble_distance(H0::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates HUbble distance (i.e., size of the observable Universe) (D_H) in rm mathbfmeters.  The formula is\n\nD_H = fracrm crm H_0 \n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_distance_radial","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_distance_radial","text":"comoving_distance_radial(cosmo::AbstractCosmology, zi::RV, zf::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the comoving radial distance (D_C) between z_1 and z_2 in rm mathbfmeters. The formula is,\n\nD_C = D_H int_z_1^z_2 fracdzE(z)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_distance_transverse","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_distance_transverse","text":"comoving_distance_transverse(cosmo::AbstractCosmology, zi::RV, zf::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the comoving radial distance (D_M) between, z_1 and z_2 in rm mathbfmeters. The formula is,\n\nD_M = begincases \nD_H frac1sqrtOmega_k   sinh left sqrtOmega_k    D_C  D_H right  textif  Omega_k  0 \nD_C                                                                                           textif  Omega_k = 0 \nD_H frac1sqrtOmega_k  sin left sqrtOmega_k  D_C  D_H right  textif  Omega_k  0 \nendcases\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.luminosity_distance","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.luminosity_distance","text":"luminosity_distance(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the luminosity distance (D_L) to redshift z in rm mathbfmeters.  The formula is,\n\nD_L(z) = (1+z) D_M(z)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.angular_diameter_distance","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.angular_diameter_distance","text":"angular_diameter_distance(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, z1::RV, z2::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the angular diameter distance (D_A) between redshifts z_1 and z_2 in rm mathbfmeters.  The formula is,\n\nD_A(z_1 z_2) = fracD_M(z_1 z_2)1+z_2\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.distance_modulus","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.distance_modulus","text":"distance_modulus(cosmo::AbstractCosmology, zf::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the distance modulus (mu) to a given redshift z.  The formula is,\n\nmu = 5 logleft( fracD_Lrm pc right) - 5\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.angular_scale","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.angular_scale","text":"angular_scale(cosmo::AbstractCosmology, zf::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the angular size in rm mathbfKpc for 1 on sky at redhsift, z.  The formula is\n\nd = 1 times left( fracD_Armkpc right)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#Volumes","page":"Cosmology","title":"Volumes","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_volume_element","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_volume_element","text":"comoving_volume_element(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, zf::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the comving volume element (dV_C) at redshift z in rm mathbfGpc^3. The formula is\n\ndV_C = D_H fracD_M^2(z)E(z)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology/#LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_volume","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_volume","text":"comoving_volume(cosmology::AbstractCosmology, zf::RV)::RV\n\nCalculates the total comving volume up to redshift z in rm mathbfGpc^3. The formula is,\n\nV_C = begincases \nfrac4pi2 fracD_H^3Omega_k   left fracD_MD_H sqrt1+Omega_k left(fracD_MD_Hright)^2 \n      - frac1sqrtOmega_k rm arcsinhleft( sqrtOmega_k fracD_MD_H  right) right  textif  Omega_k  0 \nfrac4pi3 D_M^3                                                   textif  Omega_k = 0 \nfrac4pi2 fracD_H^3Omega_k left fracD_MD_H sqrt1+Omega_k left(fracD_MD_Hright)^2 \n      - frac1sqrtOmega_k arcsinleft( sqrtOmega_k fracD_MD_H  right) right  textif  Omega_k  0 \nendcases\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Lenses/#LensFactory.Lenses","page":"Basics","title":"LensFactory.Lenses","text":"Lenses\n\nTesting :-)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"Lenses/#LensFactory.Lenses.get_meshgrid","page":"Basics","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.get_meshgrid","text":"get_meshgrid(θx::RV, θy::RV, dθ::RV) --> Tuple{Matrix{<:Float64}, Matrix{<:Float64}}\n\nGenerate a meshgrid of coordinates on which various quantities can be evaluated.\n(-θx, -θy) +--- dθ --- dθ ---+ (+θx, -θy)\n           |        |        |\n           dθ       |        dθ\n           |        |        |\n           +--- dθ --- dθ ---+\n           |        |        |\n           dθ       |        dθ\n           |        |        |\n(-θx, +θy) +--- dθ --- dθ ---+ (+θx, +θy)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Lenses/#LensFactory.Lenses.get_critical_density","page":"Basics","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.get_critical_density","text":"get_critical_density(Dd::RV, Dds::RV, Ds::RV; unit=\"kg_m2\")::RV\n\nCalculate the critical surface density (Sigma_rm cr) given the angular diameter distances. The result can be returned in different units:  \"kg_m2\" rm (i  e  kgm^2),  \"msun_pc2\" rm (i  e  M_odotpc^2),  or \"msun_arcsec2\" rm (i  e  M_odotarcsec^2).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Lenses/#LensFactory.Lenses.get_potential","page":"Basics","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.get_potential","text":"get_potential(lens::AbstractLens, θ_x::ROA, θ_y::ROA) --> ROA\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Lenses/#LensFactory.Lenses.get_deflection","page":"Basics","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.get_deflection","text":"get_deflection(lens::AbstractLens, θ_x::ROA, θ_y::ROA) --> Tuple{ROA, ROA}\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Lenses/#LensFactory.Lenses.get_jacobian","page":"Basics","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.get_jacobian","text":"get_jacobian(lens::AbstractLens, θ_x::ROA, θ_y::ROA) --> Tuple{ROA, ROA, ROA}\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"PointLens/#LensFactory.Lenses.init_PointLens","page":"Point Lens","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.init_PointLens","text":"init_PointLens(D_d::Real=NaN, x_c::Real=0.0, y_c::Real=0.0, mass::Real=NaN)\n\nInitialize a point lens with the given parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"PointLens/#LensFactory.Lenses.PointLens.potential!","page":"Point Lens","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.PointLens.potential!","text":"potential!(ψ::T, θx::T, θy::T, Dol::RV, θxc::RV, θyc::RV, mass::RV) where {T <: ROA}\n\npsi(pmbtheta) = frac4rm GMrm c^2 frac1D_d ln pmbtheta - pmbtheta_c\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"PointLens/#LensFactory.Lenses.PointLens.deflection!","page":"Point Lens","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.PointLens.deflection!","text":"deflection!(ψx::T, ψy::T, θx::T, θy::T, Dol::RV, θxc::RV, θyc::RV, mass::RV) where {T <: ROA}\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"PointLens/#LensFactory.Lenses.PointLens.jacobian!","page":"Point Lens","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.PointLens.jacobian!","text":"jacobian!(ψxx::T, ψyy::T, ψxy::T, θx::T, θy::T, Dol::RV, θxc::RV, θyc::RV, mass::RV) where {T <: ROA}\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"PointLens/#LensFactory.Lenses.PointLens.einstein_angle","page":"Point Lens","title":"LensFactory.Lenses.PointLens.einstein_angle","text":"einstein_angle(Dol::RV, Dls::RV, Dos::RV, mass::RV)::RV\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#LensFactory.jl","page":"Home","title":"LensFactory.jl","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Documentation for LensFactory.jl","category":"page"},{"location":"#LensFactory","page":"Home","title":"LensFactory","text":"LensFactory\n\nTesting :-)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"}]
